<title>FRANCE: Algeria bought durum wheat, probably Canadian.</title>
<headline>Algeria bought durum wheat, probably Canadian.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria recently bought several cargoes of durum wheat, probably Canadian, at prices ranging from $210 to $215 per tonne, cost and freight, European grain exporters said.</p>
<p>&quot;Algeria bought several cargoes of durum wheat but we do not know the exact tonnage involved,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Algeria was initially seeking 100,000 tonnes of optional durum wheat for shipment in May and June. But exporters said it may have purchased less than 100,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
